COMMON TRAPS

- ⚠️ Individual Rates vs. ROR: Individual rates (-ΔA/Δt) do NOT include coefficients. ROR divides by them.
- ⚠️ Elementary Trap: Only assume molecularity = order if "elementary" is explicitly stated.
- ⚠️ Unit Mismatch: Always check if Eₐ is in kJ or J when using R = 8.314 (J).
- ⚠️ Pseudo Order: Water concentration is constant (solvent); ignore it in 1st order rate law.
- ⚠️ log vs ln: Use 2.303 when switching from natural log (ln) to log₁₀.
- ⚠️ T dependence of Radioactive Decay: Trap! Eₐ = 0 for decay, so rate constant doesn't depend on T.
- ⚠️ Gaseous ROR: Never put P_total directly into log. Must calculate P_reactant.

